{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Why\nEpic polite-antivirus-bedbug (`536b-8930-b922-4063`) has an acceptance box that reads: \"docs/concurrency.md §I1 moved 'implemented'; residual pack size quantified; W3 set; W1/W2 filed\". On origin/main 9d10232dd89, two places are out of date:\n- docs/concurrency.md §I1 (lines 61-75) still says the reclamation \"is specified by **ADR 0106**\".\n- ADR 0106 `## Follow-up` (lines 222-225) still says \"*specified, in-progress*\".\n\nThe reclamation was run on production `tickets` on 2026-11-20 at 18:14 PST. The sources for every figure are in this ticket's comment \"Fact sources\".\n\n## What changes\nDocs only. No code, config key, env var, flag or test changes.\n1. In docs/concurrency.md §I1, replace the \"**`.retired` lifecycle.**\" text, from line 61 up to (not including) \"`.retired` files are **benign under a code rollback**\", with the block below, committed exactly as written (same line breaks). The rollback sentence and everything after it stay unchanged, as a new paragraph. This removes the old sentence \"the pack the CI budget guards is blobless\". That sentence is wrong today: the budget measures only the code checkout (cc4a23a2405).\n\n```markdown\n**`.retired` lifecycle.** Retired files stay in the working tree permanently. That\nstorage tradeoff guarantees a folded source is never lost and can never be resurrected\ninto a `SNAPSHOT_INCONSISTENT`. No branch-wide `.retired` sweep exists. Story\n`mystical-capsizable-ibis` was closed wontfix by operator decision on 2026-11-18,\nbecause the real-data dry run reached its pack reduction without one and the\nsweep's plan review blocked on fsck `SNAPSHOT_MISSING_SOURCES`, snapshot-rebuild\nrefusal and retired-event readers. The pack lever is\n**remote-anchored below-horizon commit/tree history reclamation** (ADR 0106,\n`docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md`), and it is implemented.\nIt is safe only past causal stability, meaning once no clone can still be\nmid-reconvergence against the pre-compaction events. ADR 0106 makes that condition\nprecise as the C1–C5 boundary at the commit/tree level. The implementation is split\nacross 7 modules:\n- `rebar._store.reclaim_eligibility`: the `[reclaim].horizon_days` remote-reachability check.\n- `rebar._commands.reclaim_collapse`: the core-git collapse, with authorship-ledger\n  `position→commit_sha` re-resolution and the `enforce_since` re-anchor.\n- `rebar._commands.reclaim_collapse_stream`: the long-lived `fast-import` and\n  `cat-file` sessions the collapse runs on.\n- `rebar._commands.reclaim_resign`: re-signs failing events during the collapse.\n- `rebar._commands.reclaim_publish`: the lease-guarded publish-swap, the S3 bundle-set\n  replacement, and rollback.\n- `rebar._commands.reclaim_dry_run`: the shadow-clone dry-run harness.\n- `rebar._store.stale_override`: the reconnect override.\n\nThe reconnect and publish protocols are the paragraphs \"Reconnect after a history\nreclaim\" and \"Publishing a reclaimed baseline\" under Inbound — background sync.\nThe reclamation was run on 2026-11-20 at 18:14 PST, under epic `polite-antivirus-bedbug`\n(`536b-8930-b922-4063`). It was one lease-guarded atomic push that moved `tickets` from\n`efcf5ae2b97` to `6a6dda16fc7`, and it left the backup ref\n`refs/tickets-backup/pre-reclaim-20261121T021044Z` at the old tip. Commits went from\n312,156 to 14,235. On the proof's fake remote, the blobless pack went from\n625 MiB to 108 MiB. **Measured residual:** a fresh blobless bare clone of origin\n`tickets` at `4fd8b099490` (14,375 commits), taken 2026-11-20 at 21:13 PST, has\n`size-pack` 122,794 KiB (about 120 MiB). The residual grows with write volume until\nthe next reclaim. No CI budget applies to it: the `verify-identity.yml` pack budget\n(102,400 KiB) measures only the code checkout, which excludes `tickets` (`cc4a23a2405`).\n```\n\n2. Replace the single paragraph of ADR 0106 `## Follow-up` (lines 222-225) with:\n\n```markdown\n`docs/concurrency.md` §I1's `.retired` lifecycle note is promoted from a *follow-up* to an\n*implemented* model. It cross-references this ADR as the reclamation contract and records\nthe 2026-11-20 production run and its measured residual pack. Implementation was delivered\nby stories **S1** (collapse engine + ledger reconciliation), **S2** (publish-swap + rollback)\nand **S3** (dry-run harness) under epic `536b`.\n```\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\nProofs run from the worktree root. `I1` means the output of `sed -n '/^### I1/,/^### I2/p' docs/concurrency.md`.\n- [ ] I1 states the reclamation is implemented: `grep -c 'and it is implemented'` over I1 prints 1.\n- [ ] I1 names all 7 modules. Each of these greps at least once in I1:\n  - `reclaim_eligibility`\n  - `reclaim_collapse\\``\n  - `reclaim_collapse_stream`\n  - `reclaim_resign`\n  - `reclaim_publish`\n  - `reclaim_dry_run`\n  - `stale_override`\n- [ ] I1 points to the 2 existing paragraphs: I1 contains `under Inbound — background sync`, and `grep -c 'Reconnect after a history reclaim (ADR 0106\\|Publishing a reclaimed baseline, and rolling it back' docs/concurrency.md` prints 2.\n- [ ] I1 records the run. I1 contains each of:\n  - `2026-11-20 at 18:14 PST`\n  - `efcf5ae2b97`\n  - `6a6dda16fc7`\n  - `refs/tickets-backup/pre-reclaim-20261121T021044Z`\n  - `312,156`\n  - `14,235`\n  - `625 MiB to 108 MiB`\n- [ ] I1 records the measured residual. I1 contains each of `122,794 KiB`, `4fd8b099490`, `14,375 commits`, `grows with write volume` and `cc4a23a2405`.\n- [ ] I1 gives the recorded wontfix reason. I1 contains `mystical-capsizable-ibis` and `operator decision on 2026-11-18`.\n- [ ] The old wording is gone. Each of these prints 0:\n  - `grep -cF 'is specified by **ADR 0106**' docs/concurrency.md`\n  - `grep -cF 'the pack the CI budget guards is blobless' docs/concurrency.md`\n- [ ] The rollback sentence survives: I1 contains `benign under a code rollback`.\n- [ ] Only the planned regions change:\n  - `git diff -U0 origin/main --stat` lists exactly the 2 files.\n  - Every concurrency.md hunk starts at a line from 61 to 80.\n  - Every ADR hunk starts at line 222 or later.\n- [ ] The ADR Follow-up is updated: in the ADR, `grep -c 'specified, in-progress'` prints 0 and `grep -c '\\*implemented\\* model'` prints 1.\n- [ ] `make verify` passes, or each failure is shown to be environmental.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The Gerrit change gets `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1` on its current patch set with 0 unresolved comments, and it merges to main. Evidence on this ticket: change number, patch-set SHA, votes and the merged SHA on origin/main.\n  provenance: environment=developer-workstation-worktree; principal=RebarBotNava; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — votes are read from the Gerrit REST API, and the merge is confirmed with `git branch -r --contains`.\n\n## File impact\n- docs/concurrency.md: the §I1 paragraph only.\n- docs/adr/0106-remote-anchored-history-reclamation.md: the Follow-up paragraph only.\n\n## Portability\nDocs only. Nothing depends on a CI provider.\n\n## Testing\nDocs only, so no new test. The AC commands are the proof, run before commit. `make verify` covers the docs-drift, ADR-index and doc-policy tests."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795240162864573001,"uuid":"772dfed9-7bf5-4331-8200-9db31e3b504a"}